  "caption": "Irish Revenue sets two presence tests: 183 days or more in a tax year, or 280 days or more across the current and preceding tax years together.\n\nRevenue also states that you will not be resident if you are there for 30 days or less in a tax year. A tax year runs from 1 January to 31 December.\n\nThese are residence tests, not a calculation of all tax liabilities. Check the full rules before planning a move.\n\nSource: Irish Revenue: residence for tax purposes.\nhttps://www.revenue.ie/en/jobs-and-pensions/tax-residence/resident-for-tax-purposes.aspx\n\nPhoto: Paphos Castle, Cyprus, Bukvoed, CC BY 4.0 (cropped).\nhttps://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cyprus-Paphos-Castle-0957.jpg\nhttps://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0\n\n#Cyprus #Relocation #Tax #Ireland #TheSmartySolution",
